WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.680
NHTSA proposal removes manual lighting rules for vehicles like cybercab without steering wheels or pedals. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 644. Semi-production, lfp cells, and megapacks in Belgium come next, plus counterpoint and first principles. The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration, or NHTSA, is aiming the file at vehicles built only for automated driving systems, according to a Tesla Motors sub-reddit report of the proposal.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:35.480
That proposal also adds optional cyan exterior lights to mark unsupervised operation.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:38.600
Headlight testing voltages would be adjusted as well.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:42.660
The federal register is scheduled to carry it on October 26th.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:45.400
A 30-day comment period follows publication.

00:00:46.473 --> 00:00:48.513
Volume output of the semi is underway.

00:00:49.253 --> 00:00:54.833
Yahoo Finance says Tesla is putting $2.8 billion into AI-related components for that truck

00:00:54.833 --> 00:00:55.373
program.

00:00:55.373 --> 00:01:02.373
lithium-iron phosphate, or LFP, battery production has a Tesla allocation, bar chart reported.

00:01:02.913 --> 00:01:04.673
The figure is $4.3 billion.

00:01:06.052 --> 00:01:08.672
Belgium has taken delivery of Tesla Megapax.

00:01:09.152 --> 00:01:14.472
The storage installation is sized at 400 megawatt hours, according to Drive Tesla Canada.

00:01:15.152 --> 00:01:18.972
Giga Berlin produced 7,000 model Y vehicles in a single week.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:24.452
Optimus production quality builds have started on a free-mont line size for 1 million units

00:01:24.452 --> 00:01:31.552
a year. Tesla Roddy reports, an Optimus Academy is planned so 10,000 to 20,000 robots can practice

00:01:31.552 --> 00:01:38.052
tasks and generate training data. Tesla expects to install its AI-5 chip in Optimus next year.

00:01:38.712 --> 00:01:45.943
External deliveries are aimed by the end of 2027. Yulin China has a new Tesla showroom at Wanda Plaza,

00:01:46.663 --> 00:01:51.083
TSL aiming posted. A cyber truck on display there drew large crowds.

00:01:51.083 --> 00:01:51.243
clouds.

00:01:51.683 --> 00:01:53.863
Neighboring auto-brands stand stayed empty.

00:01:54.503 --> 00:01:59.123
Japan will get vehicle-to-load power export on new Model 3 and Model Y vehicles.

00:01:59.703 --> 00:02:05.603
A Tesla motor subreddit post said, an adapter price at 15,000 yen is slated to go on sale

00:02:05.603 --> 00:02:07.783
starting January 2027.

00:02:08.807 --> 00:02:14.387
Tesla Rade released a 34-second video of the Roadster touchscreen shown before thruster activation.

00:02:14.847 --> 00:02:19.267
The layout takes fighter jet cues and centers on a three-dimensional model of the car.

00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:25.727
Home, vehicle, listen, climate, and navigate appear as tabs. Track mode shows circuit

00:02:25.727 --> 00:02:31.387
maps, lap times, temperatures, and tire data. Arrow mode selectors sit beside a thruster

00:02:31.387 --> 00:02:37.647
gauge at 5,500 psi, and a boost-ready light linked to cold gas thrusters for the thrust

00:02:37.647 --> 00:02:43.567
and rocket variants. Production is slated for 2028, and the rocket version is restricted

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:49.350
from public roads. Tesla and SpaceX are forming merger committees that reports say would need

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:52.630
a 50% shareholder vote, according to Tech Insider.

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:56.750
Those reports also reference tariffab chips in the combined entity.

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:00.470
Rivian is buying an AI startup, Stock Twits reported.

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:06.690
GM and Ford are advancing their own EV plans in that same roundup, which also cited reported

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:07.730
profit declines.

00:03:08.694 --> 00:03:15.934
One driver reported a new personal record streak on full self-driving, or FSD, version 14.3.13.

00:03:15.934 --> 00:03:21.334
That driver said the system is learning new behaviors. A high mileage Model 3 reached

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:28.014
250,000 miles with only one part replaced according to Tech Insider. Optimus volume targets

00:03:28.014 --> 00:03:32.794
of 20,000 units per week are being compared with current production realities in that coverage.

00:03:33.374 --> 00:03:39.314
An owner was quoted $10,000 for repairs on a Model S. The trade in offer on that car came

00:03:39.314 --> 00:03:45.734
in at $8,500. The cooldown reported. High repair estimates in that case can push an owner

00:03:45.734 --> 00:03:50.774
toward replacement rather than continued maintenance. Tesla has not commented on the specific

00:03:50.774 --> 00:03:56.750
incident. Lithium iron phosphate gives up some energy density to buy a lower cost per kilowatt

00:03:56.750 --> 00:04:02.110
hour and more thermal stability. That trade matters when the same cells have to cover daily driving

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:07.850
cycles and stationary packs that cycle less often. Stationary packs still have to last decades.

00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:13.970
Higher density packs still run into cobalt and nickel constraints. Semi-volume depends on whether

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:16.570
other LFP supply can grow without those constraints.

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:22.550
Dedicated LFP lines would set a cost floor under payload economics and under later stationary

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:24.370
projects that use the same cells.

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:29.810
The parallel spend on AI silicon inside the truck treats the vehicle as a rolling inference

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:31.810
node rather than a simple transporter.

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:37.350
Cheaper cells plus onboard compute is the pairing that would have to undercut diesel total cost

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:40.290
of ownership on long haul routes before 2028.

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:44.930
The same chemistry also changes the risk profile for stationary projects.

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:49.750
Those packs can take deeper discharge cycles and higher ambient temperatures without

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:51.990
the degradation curves of nickel-rich cells.

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:57.590
That stability matters when a utility size is a system for multi-hour arbitrage instead

00:04:57.590 --> 00:04:59.610
of short bursts of frequency regulation.

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:03.290
The LFP spend then works as shared infrastructure.

00:05:03.890 --> 00:05:08.850
The cells that lower a truck's bill of materials also cut replacement frequency in grid assets

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:10.470
that must run for 20 years.

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:14.350
When the two programs draw from overlapping supply contracts,

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:16.710
a delay in LFP line construction

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:19.970
hits the truck program and the Megapack backlog at once.

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:24.170
Academy robots add another claim on that same capital stack.

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:27.230
Each robot is discussed against AI5.

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:29.570
The Silicon family also referenced

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:31.390
in the semi-AI component budget.

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:35.510
If LFP sells power the truck in future stationary buffers

00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:37.230
for Dojo scale training clusters,

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:42.350
The chemistry becomes the common denominator across mobility, robotics, and compute.

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:46.730
Lower energy density can still impose a payload or runtime penalty.

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:52.630
That penalty would show up once robots leave controlled academy tasks for unstructured factory floors.

00:05:53.090 --> 00:06:01.224
Before we go, any fresh detail on tariffab chips inside a combined Tesla Space X entity is the next marker on that committee thread.

00:06:01.864 --> 00:06:04.004
And that's a wrap on today's Tesla news.

